        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Leuctra</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">6 July 371 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Near Leuctra, a village in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a> in the territory of Thespiae, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Boeotians led by the Thebans, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epaminondas">Epaminondas</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pelopidas">Pelopidas</a> commanding the Sacred Band of 300, against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> and its allies under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleombrotus-i">Cleombrotus I</a>; the general modern consensus is about 7,000 Boeotian infantry and 700 cavalry against about 10,000 Peloponnesian infantry, including 700 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spartiates">Spartiates</a>, and 1,000 cavalry, though the ancient sources nearly all disagree</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Thebans broke the Spartan right wing, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleombrotus-i">Cleombrotus</a> was mortally wounded and the Spartans and their allies fled; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xenophon">Xenophon</a> puts Spartan dead at almost 1,000, about 400 of them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spartiates">Spartiates</a>.</span></div>
